# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the CVFit Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version ^2.0.0 to dependencies
- **Modified**: `package.json` to include the new dependency
- **Updated**: `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Configuration
- **Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next';`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the ThemeProvider closing tag
  - Follows Next.js App Router pattern as documented in the official quickstart guide

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide for Next.js App Router:
1. Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
2. Identified the project as Next.js App Router (v16.1.6) based on the presence of `app/layout.tsx`
3. Used npm (project's package manager) to install the package
4. Added the SpeedInsights component to the root layout as recommended for App Router

## Placement Rationale
The `<SpeedInsights />` component is placed:
- Inside the `<body>` tag for proper tracking
- After all other providers and content (ThemeProvider, TooltipProvider, AuthProvider, etc.)
- This ensures it doesn't interfere with existing functionality while properly tracking page performance

## Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed with no errors
- ✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing warnings are pre-existing)
- ✅ All static and dynamic routes built correctly

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Data will begin collecting automatically once users visit the site
3. Metrics will appear in the Vercel dashboard after several days of traffic

## Files Modified
- `frontend-next/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend-next/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `frontend-next/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component and import
